<capabilities>
<p>The Nagasawa is a 3,000-ton military aerodyne assault DropShip created by enlarging the Noruff hull by roughly fifty percent. Its drive system provides a safe thrust of 8, giving the vessel the speed to place itself between a threat and the ship it protects and to dictate the range of an engagement. Ninety tons of Ferro-Aluminum armor, concentrated heavily on the nose, allow the Nagasawa to absorb punishment that would force a lighter escort out of the line. The weapons suite is deliberately straightforward: a nose battery of ER PPCs and rotary autocannons, wing batteries of ER Large Lasers and Artemis V-guided LRM 20 launchers, and an aft arc of ER Large and Large Pulse Lasers. This mix of energy, ballistic, and missile fire ensures that no single advanced armor type can blunt the vessel's offensive potential. Fifteen laser anti-missile systems spread across the wings and aft provide dependable point defense with no ammunition to run dry. The design was engineered for ease of maintenance, with accessible components that reduce time spent in the yards. Like its Noruff progenitor, however, the Nagasawa cannot enter an atmosphere, restricting it to orbital and deep-space operations, and its modest cargo bay and single small craft cubicle offer little transport utility.</p>
</capabilities>

<overview>
<p>The Nagasawa is an assault DropShip developed by Clan Sea Fox to defend the ArcShips at the heart of its merchant aimags. Aerospace fighters alone had proven insufficient to protect these vital trade vessels, and the Sea Foxes sought a dedicated escort able to meet any threat on equal terms. Building on the proven Noruff design, Sea Fox engineers produced an enlarged, heavily protected vessel that entered service in 3115 from Fox's Warren Naval Yard on Tukayyid. The Nagasawa quickly became a common sight around the Sea Fox aimags, and its reputation as a capable and dependable escort has made it one of the more sought-after Clan DropShip designs of the Dark Age. Few captains choose to challenge a trading fleet sheltering under its guns.</p>
</overview>

<deployment>
<p>The standard Nagasawa serves in its baseline escort configuration, screening ArcShips and other high-value vessels for Clan Sea Fox naval formations. Escorts typically position themselves between the protected vessel and an approaching threat, using their superior thrust and heavy armor to draw enemy fire and stay clear of sub-capital weaponry while their mixed battery wears down the opponent. Outside the Sea Fox fleet, Nagasawas acquired through purchase or Trial serve as screening vessels for heavier DropShips and WarShips, and their modest cost allows commanders to assign them to duties that would not otherwise warrant a dedicated DropShip escort.</p>
</deployment>

<history>
<p>Clan Sea Fox developed the Nagasawa in the early thirty-second century to give its ArcShip fleet a dedicated escort. Rather than design an entirely new hull, Sea Fox engineers enlarged the Noruff by roughly half, retaining much of its speed while adding the protection and firepower an escort required, and built the vessel with the maintenance needs of Sea Fox crews firmly in mind. Production began at Fox's Warren Naval Yard on Tukayyid, and the first Nagasawas entered service in 3115.</p><p>The class did not remain a Sea Fox exclusive for long. Through sales and Trials, Nagasawas found their way into the toumans of every Clan. Even Clan Wolf, which produces the competing Isegrim, and Clan Jade Falcon, with its substantial WarShip fleet, have fielded several, while the remaining Clans have eagerly acquired any Nagasawas made available to screen their heavier vessels.</p><p>The design proved itself over Symington, where two Nagasawas of the Rasalhague Dominion engaged the Jade Falcon corvette Jade Tornado and its escorting carrier. While the opposing fighters fought to a stalemate, the Nagasawas pressed directly toward the corvette, forcing it to concentrate its fire on them and allowing the Dominion's heavier DropShips to attack unhindered. One Nagasawa absorbed a direct hit and remained in the fight, and after ten minutes Jade Tornado withdrew. Both DropShips returned to full operational status within a fortnight.</p><p>When the Capellan Confederation's Operation CELESTIAL REWARD brought mounting pressure on Skate Khanate affiliates for war materiel, saKhan Sennet assigned Nagasawa escorts to the most important of them. In one notable action, a single Nagasawa intercepted a Lung Wang-class DropShip closing on a JumpShip under its protection. Though outgunned, the escort used its armor and thrust advantages to stay clear of the Capellan vessel's sub-capital weapons, disabled its drive, and destroyed its fighter screen before claiming the crippled DropShip as isorla. Nagasawa captains have also built a formidable record in Trials, with at least one Tiburon Khanate vessel amassing nineteen victories without defeat despite bidding away much of its armament.</p>
</history>

